<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/storm-roof-damage.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/storm-roof-damage-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/storm-roof-damage.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="771" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/">Services</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Wind &amp; Tornado Damage Appraisal</span></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Wind and Tornado Damage Appraisal in Virginia</h1><p class="lede">Virginia doesn’t need a hurricane to see major wind losses. Derechos, squall lines and short-lived tornadoes tear off shingles, siding and porch roofs every year.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Common sources</dt><dd>Derechos, squall lines</dd></div><div><dt>Tornado season</dt><dd>Spring &amp; tropical remnants</dd></div><div><dt>Typical gap</dt><dd>Hidden &amp; framing damage</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Wind events Virginia actually gets</h2>
<p>The June 2012 derecho swept across the state in a few hours, knocking out power for well over a million Virginia customers and dropping trees and roofs from the Shenandoah Valley to the Chesapeake Bay. Tornadoes are less frequent than in the Plains, but they do strike. The February 2016 outbreak hit Appomattox County and the town of Waverly, and the remnants of Tropical Storm Isaias spawned a deadly tornado in Southampton County in August 2020. Many Virginia tornadoes form inside tropical systems and squall lines, so they arrive with little warning.</p>
<h2>What a wind and tornado damage appraisal looks for</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Creased and unsealed shingles</strong> that stay in place but have lost their bond. They’re easy to miss from the ground and often left out of the first estimate.</li>
<li><strong>Siding and trim</strong> where a few missing pieces mean a full elevation can’t be matched.</li>
<li><strong>Structural movement</strong>: racked porches, shifted trusses, cracked rafters and damaged sheathing.</li>
<li><strong>Outbuildings, fences and carports</strong> under Other Structures coverage.</li>
<li><strong>Interior water</strong> from wind-driven rain entering through the damaged envelope.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Deductibles and causation</h2>
<p>Some Virginia policies carry a separate wind or named-storm deductible, often a percentage of dwelling coverage. When a tornado forms inside a named tropical system, which deductible applies depends on the policy’s trigger language. We read that wording before the dollars are argued. Our <a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/hurricane-wind-deductible-converter/">deductible converter</a> shows what a percentage deductible means in dollars.</p>
<h3>Wear versus wind</h3>
<p>Carriers often attribute lifted or missing shingles to age. We separate pre-existing wear from fresh storm damage with tear patterns, debris fields, fastener evidence and local weather data for your address.</p>
<h2>Questions about wind &amp; tornado damage appraisal</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How do I prove the wind speed at my house?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Official stations are often miles away. Storm reports, radar data, damage surveys and nearby damage patterns help establish what happened at your address.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is a derecho treated like a hurricane under my policy?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually not. Named-storm deductibles normally depend on a storm named by the National Hurricane Center or a related warning. A derecho is a windstorm, so your standard or wind deductible would typically apply.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="related"><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/hurricane-and-noreaster-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Hurricane &amp; Nor’easter Appraisal</span></a><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/water-damage-claim-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Water Damage Claim Appraisal</span></a><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/fire-and-smoke-damage-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</span></a></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-h">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="box-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-accent btn-block" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Send claim details</a><p class="box-small">Mon–Fri 8am–6pm ET · All of Virginia</p></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-h">All services</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/homeowners-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowners Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/commercial-and-hoa-claim-appraisal/">Co